# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensed and non-public raw data.
#
# This repository is public. Raw data that is not itself public must not be
# accessible through it. Sources marked `can_commit_raw: false` in
# config/sources.yml belong here; stewards keep their local copies outside git,
# or under the directory named by EIG_MANUAL_DIR.
#
# Only the manifest entry for these sources is committed -- the vintage, hash,
# row count and schema fingerprint in data/_state/manifest.csv. That is enough
# to prove which version produced a published number without redistributing the
# payload.
#
# Removing a path here does NOT remove it from git history. See
# docs/refactor_plan.md F-13.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# BloombergNEF -- commercial subscription, redistribution prohibited
data/raw/BNEF/

# Good Jobs First Subsidy Tracker -- redistribution not permitted
data/raw/Good Jobs First/

# CNBC America's Top States for Business -- editorial content, redistribution
# not permitted. Untracked 2026-10-01; cnbc_rank falls back to base_inputs on a
# clean clone. Steward instructions and a template are in config/sources.yml.
data/raw/cnbc_bus_rankings.csv

# C2ER State Business Incentives Database -- commercial subscription,
# redistribution not permitted. Untracked 2026-10-01; dev_policy_count falls
# back to base_inputs on a clean clone.
data/raw/dbo_Program.csv

# Belt and braces: catch these payloads wherever they are dropped.
#
# The leading `*` matters. This repository lives inside a synced OneDrive
# folder, and sync tools write conflict copies beside the original:
# `dbo_Program(1).csv`, `cnbc_bus_rankings - Copy.csv`, `gjf_complete-DESKTOP.csv`.
# An exact-name rule does not match those, so on 2026-10-19 a conflict copy of
# the C2ER payload was sitting untracked and NOT ignored -- one `git add -A`
# from a public repository. Globbing both sides catches every variant.
**/*Global Data Center Live IT Capacity Database*
*gjf_complete*
*dbo_Program*
*cnbc_bus_rankings*

# Sync-conflict copies of anything under data/raw, whatever its licence. These
# are never wanted in git: the original is either tracked already or ignored on
# purpose, and a copy is at best duplicate weight and at worst a leak.
data/raw/**/*(1)*
data/raw/**/*(2)*
data/raw/**/* - Copy*
data/raw/**/*-Copy*
data/raw/**/*conflicted copy*

# Manual drop payloads for licensed sources. Templates and READMEs under
# data/manual/ stay tracked; the data files do not.
data/manual/**/*.csv
data/manual/**/*.xlsx
data/manual/**/*.zip
!data/manual/**/TEMPLATE.csv
